1
00:00:15,974 --> 00:00:18,101
‎Oh... Hey, Mom.

2
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:22,564
‎Don't scare me like that.

3
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:26,192
‎What? Thought I ran away?

4
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:29,362
‎You're certain?

5
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,741
‎She's hardly in a state
‎to be moving around...

6
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:35,577
‎But it didn't seem like
‎she was struggling.

7
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:38,580
‎Especially compared to
‎when we admitted her.

8
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:40,498
‎She seems... better!

9
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:44,335
‎I see. I'll stop by to check on her.

10
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:49,090
‎She just... really... seems so normal today.

11
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:52,635
‎Is there any chance
‎she might recover on her own?

12
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,347
‎I understand your desire to think so.

13
00:00:56,431 --> 00:01:00,101
‎However...
‎And it pains me to have to say this.

14
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:05,065
‎Terminal patients sometimes
‎appear to improve temporarily.

15
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:11,446
‎It can give the family hope,
‎but more often than not... soon after that...

16
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:14,407
‎I... understand.

17
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:18,323
‎Roman.

18
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:20,491
‎Lend me your computer.

19
00:03:29,250 --> 00:03:30,460
‎You're selfish.

20
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:34,631
‎My deck doesn't have
‎enough processing punch.

21
00:03:35,381 --> 00:03:37,050
‎What're you making?

22
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:38,509
‎Something I need.

23
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:41,346
‎Didn't think you were ever comin' back.

24
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:43,932
‎I tried lookin' for you.

25
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:46,059
‎Where'd you go?

26
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:49,479
‎If you want the chip... Not happenin'.

27
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:53,566
‎At least not yet... Okay, done.

28
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:59,530
‎You had your cam rollin'
‎when I was tanglin' with 'Saka, right?

29
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:01,157
‎Show me the footage.

30
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:13,044
‎-Is that it?
‎-Yeah.

31
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:16,047
‎You didn't film to the end?

32
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,215
‎Couldn't.

33
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:22,553
‎Well... guess this'll work.

34
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:23,846
‎What do you mean?

35
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,765
‎I want you to cut a reel for me.

36
00:04:25,848 --> 00:04:28,434
‎Make it look like
‎I dealt Arasaka a huge blow.

37
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:30,019
‎Go heavy on the gore.

38
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:32,063
‎Hold on, why do you need a reel like that?

39
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:35,441
‎The chip... you want it, don't you?

40
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:39,988
‎Lend me a hand.
‎You'll get it once I've had my revenge.

41
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:43,700
‎What's your plan?

42
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:48,871
‎Need more material...

43
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:52,542
‎-‎Why the mask?
‎-‎What's it to you?

44
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,086
‎Why're you on the ground?

45
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:57,088
‎What's it to you?

46
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,924
‎Rolling.

47
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:04,887
‎To the Arasaka butchers
‎who slaughtered my clan!

48
00:05:04,971 --> 00:05:07,807
‎Come forward now, or
‎I'll hunt down more 'Saka suits one by--

49
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:08,975
‎Hold on!

50
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:12,270
‎You're declarin' war against Arasaka?

51
00:05:12,353 --> 00:05:14,230
‎-Yeah. So what?
‎-Wait!

52
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:17,567
‎You're gonna broadcast this? Usin' Capri?

53
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,736
‎-No shit.
‎-Are you skezzed?

54
00:05:19,819 --> 00:05:22,739
‎You're free to chicken out.
‎Nothin' I can't handle solo.

55
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:25,199
‎Press record, slap some edits in there...

56
00:05:25,783 --> 00:05:27,076
‎It doesn't have to be you.

57
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:33,624
‎Dang it! Fine, I'll do it! Happy now?

58
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:17,085
‎Been a tick since we came here last.

59
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:19,879
‎Kinda feels like the early days.

60
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,548
‎Don't be corny.

61
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:26,010
‎I did some diggin'.

62
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:30,389
‎But there's no curin' the incurable.
‎Not when she's terminally ill,

63
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:34,435
‎barely hangin' onto life,
‎and with one foot in cyberpsychosis.

64
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:36,187
‎I see.

65
00:06:36,687 --> 00:06:38,439
‎At least by conventional means.

66
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,566
‎Ever heard of Soulkiller?

67
00:06:41,859 --> 00:06:45,613
‎It's tech that can copy,
‎digitize and store a person's mind.

68
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:49,075
‎Yeah... Was cooked up
‎in Arasaka's kitchen, wasn't it?

69
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:53,162
‎Thought they shelved it 'cause
‎of some kinda critical defect.

70
00:06:53,830 --> 00:07:00,378
‎Right. The chooms they tested
‎the digitization on went brain-dead.

71
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:03,881
‎Turns out you can't copy a soul.
‎Only rip it right out.

72
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:07,093
‎Explains why it's named "Soulkiller".

73
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:10,972
‎Official company line is
‎they scrapped the project.

74
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:13,516
‎So what're you gettin' at?

75
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:17,478
‎Word is 'Saka's continued the research.

76
00:07:18,354 --> 00:07:21,649
‎Couldn't copy a soul,
‎but they nailed the data capture.

77
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:26,487
‎The digitized souls...
‎they call 'em constructs.

78
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:29,907
‎Even got close to transferrin' one
‎to a different person's body.

79
00:07:30,908 --> 00:07:32,243
‎So what I'm gettin' at...

80
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:34,495
‎Say we get our mitts on this wondertech,

81
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:37,748
‎we can scoop out the girl's soul
‎and drop it in a new body.

82
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:41,043
‎The disease may be incurable,
‎but her soul's fine.

83
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:43,254
‎This sounds unreal.

84
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:45,882
‎Hold on.

85
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:49,760
‎"They got close" means
‎it hasn't actually worked yet?

86
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:51,804
‎And that's the bitch of it.

87
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:55,266
‎Got nothin' to go on besides whispers.

88
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:57,643
‎Including rumors
‎of the lead dev bein' a flatline.

89
00:07:58,269 --> 00:08:02,523
‎That, or sold out to Kang Tao.
‎Hard to say for sure.

90
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:06,152
‎If there's real proof to be found,

91
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:08,613
‎it's buried under layers
‎of corp firewalls.

92
00:08:09,906 --> 00:08:11,574
‎Sold out to Kang Tao...

93
00:08:12,116 --> 00:08:13,451
‎What about Kang Tao?

94
00:08:14,243 --> 00:08:15,536
‎If that rumor's true...

95
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,288
‎Know a way to dig deeper.

96
00:08:37,558 --> 00:08:40,269
‎Talia! Talia! Talia!

97
00:08:40,811 --> 00:08:43,856
‎Talia! Are you okay?

98
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,942
‎What're you doing out here?

99
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:47,735
‎How'd you get this far?

100
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:52,198
‎I'll hunt down more 'Saka suits
‎one by one!

101
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:54,158
‎This is what I've got...

102
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:55,993
‎Better than I expected.

103
00:08:56,661 --> 00:09:00,706
‎Nifty work. Just be sure to include
‎this netpage address at the end.

104
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,500
‎What is it?

105
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:03,793
‎A tipline. Untraceable.

106
00:09:03,876 --> 00:09:06,963
‎Leaves no digital scat
‎for trackers to follow.

107
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:09,549
‎You made this?

108
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:10,633
‎Uh-huh.

109
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,969
‎With Capri's help.

110
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,351
‎We really gonna do this?

111
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:22,853
‎Damn right.

112
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:39,412
‎Why? Why can't I shoot you?

113
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:40,955
‎-‎Shit!
‎-Huh? What is that?

114
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:48,713
‎Ready to talk this time?

115
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:53,217
‎Speak up.

116
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:55,219
‎Street... trash.

117
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:07,398
‎To the Arasaka butchers
‎who slaughtered my clan!

118
00:10:07,481 --> 00:10:11,652
‎Come forward now, or I'll hunt down
‎more 'Saka suits one by one!

119
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:23,581
‎Well, not a bad first rodeo.

120
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:28,127
‎What's got you all nervous?

121
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:31,672
‎Wonder why.

122
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,342
‎Now Phase 2.

123
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:39,639
‎Phase 2?

124
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:43,184
‎Nomad-killin' scum, show yourselves!

125
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:18,344
‎W-wait! Please don't hurt me!

126
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:20,971
‎You know this symbol, don't you?

127
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:22,348
‎I don't know shit!

128
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:25,351
‎Don't come any closer!

129
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:26,602
‎Stop!

130
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,442
‎S-Stop.

131
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:06,892
‎Got a bit side-tracked
‎but it all worked out.

132
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:08,144
‎Um...

133
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:12,773
‎Are you the Arasaka killer guy?
‎From the vids?

134
00:12:13,607 --> 00:12:14,733
‎Who's askin'?

135
00:12:15,234 --> 00:12:17,278
‎Oh, I knew it! Knew it was you.

136
00:12:17,361 --> 00:12:18,904
‎Oh my god, you totally are!

137
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:23,409
‎I'm Yupi!

138
00:12:23,492 --> 00:12:26,495
‎Huge fan! Like, huge.

139
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,914
‎-A fan?
‎-Your vids are nova max!

140
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:33,043
‎I mean, the way you're fighting
‎Arasaka all by yourself?

141
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:36,046
‎Oh, god! It's just too much.

142
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:38,174
‎I literally can't right now.

143
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:42,178
‎So nova, gonna puke. Gonna die.

144
00:12:42,261 --> 00:12:46,390
‎There's no way
‎this is happening for real... Huh?

145
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:49,810
‎Wait! Don't go! Choomies, c'mon!

146
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:53,272
‎Seriously! Wait for me! Please!

147
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,357
‎-What?
‎-I wanna help.

148
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:58,444
‎-Let me do something. Anything!
‎-Help?

149
00:12:59,695 --> 00:13:02,740
‎Prolly shouldn't be talkin'
‎like this out in the open.

150
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:05,367
‎Come to my place!
‎It's just a skip around the corner!

151
00:13:05,951 --> 00:13:07,036
‎D, let's just go.

152
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:09,705
‎Ah, prolly don't think
‎you can trust me, huh?

153
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:11,290
‎I totally get it.

154
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:14,210
‎But I really vibe with your mission!

155
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:18,088
‎All I'm askin' for is a chance!
‎Pretty please!

156
00:13:23,719 --> 00:13:26,347
‎Here we are! Make yourselves cozy!

157
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:27,515
‎Somethin' to drink?

158
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:30,267
‎-Got any beer?
‎-Comin' up!

159
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:34,897
‎Ah! Don't!

160
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,857
‎Huh? Oh, it's probably fine...

161
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,359
‎Oh my god!

162
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:41,570
‎Wait, wait.

163
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:44,073
‎Your face! You're like... really hot!

164
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:46,492
‎What am I even looking at?!

165
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:52,206
‎Aww... That a scar? You're, like,
‎soooo close to perfect, though.

166
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:59,129
‎Where'd you get this?

167
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:02,258
‎Someone scrolled your broadcasts
‎and dropped 'em on the Net.

168
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:05,511
‎Got four of 'em so far,
‎but there's some early ones I can't find.

169
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:07,137
‎Roman's got 'em.

170
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:09,932
‎-Seriously?
‎-He's the one who made 'em.

171
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:12,768
‎For real? You made all these?

172
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:14,562
‎Seriously? You?

173
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:15,729
‎You a genius or what?

174
00:14:15,813 --> 00:14:17,398
‎One sec, got a holo.

175
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:57,187
‎Go for it. Sounds like a win.

176
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:59,440
‎-Huh.
‎-I was thinking!

177
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:01,859
‎We could build a studio here!

178
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:03,068
‎I got some spare rooms.

179
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:05,321
‎-I'll even buy you the gear!
‎-You'd do that?

180
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:08,490
‎Said I wanted to help you!

181
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:11,076
‎I friggin' hate Arasaka's guts.

182
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,621
‎Lemme fight for the cause!

183
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:15,623
‎Why do you hate 'em so much?

184
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:21,670
‎Daddy worked for 'em.
‎He ran a PR firm with lotsa corpo clients.

185
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:24,840
‎Buried a lot of crap 'Saka did.

186
00:15:25,507 --> 00:15:28,344
‎But in the end...

187
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:32,598
‎Whatever! Talk about a buzzkill!

188
00:15:32,681 --> 00:15:34,934
‎I just know they're garbo. The worst.

189
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:37,937
‎Those jerks killed
‎all your nomad choomies, didn't they?

190
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,856
‎-Yeah.
‎-Screw 'em.

191
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:44,360
‎We should burn it all to the ground.
‎Make 'em think twice!

192
00:15:45,361 --> 00:15:46,362
‎Fuckin' right.

193
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:49,657
‎And you, director!
‎Lemme know if you need any gear.

194
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,241
‎Oooh, like an editing room!

195
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:54,328
‎Um, no need to go to all that trouble.

196
00:15:54,411 --> 00:15:56,622
‎C'mon, don't be shy.

197
00:15:57,498 --> 00:16:00,292
‎Let's make this place Team D's HQ!

198
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:01,377
‎I'll drink to that.

199
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:04,380
‎Then it's settled! Cheeeers!

200
00:16:08,592 --> 00:16:10,135
‎Tick-tock, dirtbags.

201
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,680
‎Come forward, or more bodies drop.

202
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:16,266
‎You're telling me
‎we're getting countless hits,

203
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,894
‎but still can't ID
‎the motherfucker responsible?

204
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:23,482
‎These jumping IP addresses...
‎the flood of dummy traffic...

205
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:25,025
‎How can they manage so much at once?

206
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:30,656
‎The distortion on his face is
‎some kind of unknown jamming tech.

207
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:37,913
‎Whoever's behind this,
‎are they even human?

208
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:44,420
‎Whoa.

209
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:49,550
‎I'll hunt down more 'Saka suits
‎one by one!

210
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:53,929
‎Things're really startin' to blow up.

211
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:55,806
‎Huh? Yeah.

212
00:16:56,765 --> 00:16:57,766
‎Hey, D?

213
00:16:58,642 --> 00:17:00,436
‎Capri's... still around, right?

214
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:02,229
‎Why?

215
00:17:02,312 --> 00:17:04,440
‎You haven't mentioned her lately.

216
00:17:05,232 --> 00:17:07,401
‎She's here. Like always.

217
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:09,820
‎-Oh... That's good.
‎-Right?

218
00:17:46,106 --> 00:17:47,608
‎Is that...

219
00:17:49,068 --> 00:17:50,486
‎Snake Nation?

220
00:17:58,077 --> 00:17:58,994
‎Kill him!

221
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:00,829
‎Death to Arasaka scum!

222
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:04,374
‎P-please... mercy...

223
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:25,270
‎Did you leak the detes
‎on our ambush spot?

224
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:28,357
‎Guilty! And what a turnout!

225
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,858
‎Just one teensy bummer...

226
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:33,695
‎You're usin' that old hunk of junk,
‎instead of the new camera I bought ya!

227
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:36,365
‎Like, hellooo...

228
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:37,449
‎I'm goin' home.

229
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:41,620
‎Awwww. What about the edits?

230
00:18:41,703 --> 00:18:42,913
‎Tomorrow.

231
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:46,583
‎Uh, wanted those today, but whatevs.

232
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:50,254
‎Okay, that's a wrap, everyone!

233
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:05,811
‎D! D! D!

234
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:12,568
‎D! D! D! D! D! D!

235
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,741
‎Omi?

236
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:24,204
‎Wait. Omi, right?

237
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:29,960
‎Saw you back there.
‎You been doin' all right?

238
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:32,087
‎I'm getting by.

239
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:33,964
‎Yeah? Glad to hear it.

240
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:38,218
‎Have you been doing this ever since?

241
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,220
‎This?

242
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:42,055
‎This...

243
00:19:43,223 --> 00:19:44,725
‎revenge act of yours.

244
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:47,227
‎That's right.

245
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:49,688
‎All this time? Ever since that day?

246
00:19:49,771 --> 00:19:51,565
‎I finally got a lead.

247
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:53,817
‎-And it's Arasaka?
‎-Yeah.

248
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,861
‎You'd go toe-to-toe with a megacorp?

249
00:19:55,944 --> 00:19:58,071
‎In a battle you obviously can't win?!

250
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:01,825
‎What else am I supposed to do?
‎Forget what happened?

251
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:04,369
‎How'd that work out for you?

252
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:05,954
‎You know I could never forget!

253
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:08,540
‎-But resorting to revenge...
‎-You could let it go.

254
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:09,875
‎You should too!

255
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:12,794
‎Revenge won't fix anything!
‎You think it'll bring back the family?

256
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:14,171
‎They never left, Omi.

257
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:16,298
‎They're all still here.

258
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:19,801
‎They're still here...

259
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:22,679
‎and they visit every night.

260
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:24,556
‎What?

261
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:27,809
‎They come to me in my dreams.

262
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:29,561
‎I can't ever help them.

263
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:35,567
‎And getting revenge
‎is gonna make it stop?

264
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:41,323
‎They're all gonna say "good job"
‎and leave you in peace?

265
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,450
‎I dunno.

266
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:47,371
‎But they won't go away.
‎What else can I do?

267
00:20:49,998 --> 00:20:51,250
‎Sorry.

268
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:53,585
‎I shouldn't have dug up old bones.

269
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:56,004
‎See you around, Omi.

270
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:15,816
‎Who's this?

271
00:22:00,610 --> 00:22:02,779
‎Cyberware, hacking...

272
00:22:02,863 --> 00:22:07,659
‎I happen to be quite handy with
‎stuff like that, if I do say so myself.

273
00:22:37,689 --> 00:22:40,525
‎But it does seem like
‎his temper's runnin' hotter.

274
00:22:59,336 --> 00:23:02,589
‎Is it so hard to believe I love your work?

275
00:23:09,262 --> 00:23:13,475
‎So, this "Soulkiller" tech,
‎it can really save Talia?

276
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:16,895
‎Or it could just as well
‎be an urban legend.

277
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:19,981
‎But it's the only lead we got.

278
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:24,277
‎Digitize her soul
‎and put her in a new body?

279
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:26,738
‎How could this be real...

280
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:29,241
‎Went down a few rabbit holes.

281
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:31,660
‎Idea's not as far-fetched
‎as it might sound.

282
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:33,829
‎And besides...

283
00:23:33,912 --> 00:23:36,748
‎Know someone close
‎who might be able to give us a head start.

284
00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:38,500
‎Who's that?

285
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:42,337
‎Your husband.

286
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:48,510
‎It can't be...

287
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:51,263
‎Capricorn?

288
00:24:37,058 --> 00:24:39,394
‎Best I can do for now.

289
00:24:40,645 --> 00:24:41,938
‎Who're you?

290
00:24:44,065 --> 00:24:48,069
‎Hey. Wanna do something crazy?

291
00:26:19,911 --> 00:26:24,916
‎Subtitle translation by:
‎CD PROJEKT RED & Megumi Hunter
